    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Multiple Choice Questions test core conceptual clarity and application skills.",
        "Regular practice of MCQs enhances time management during competitive examinations.",
        "Systematic evaluation of each option helps eliminate incorrect distractors efficiently."
      ],
      "id": "pzxqzs8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "or9dupk",
      "content": "A potential difference of 10 V is applied across a resistor and a current of 2 A flows. The resistance of the conductor is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "y2f32at",
      "content": "A) 2 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8kbozi0",
      "content": "B) 5 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n4osg4p",
      "content": "C) 10 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "d566eia",
      "content": "D) 20 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "rdkihcn",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B (5 Ω)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "id5q22t",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p39e40e",
      "content": "Using Ohm’s Law: V = IR"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "68nu7tt",
      "content": "Rearranging: R = V / I"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "utlylou",
      "content": "Substitute values: R = 10 / 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nrlsxq1",
      "content": "R = 5 Ω"
    },
    {
      "id": "ne5p67t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8vezqk7",
      "content": "Two resistors of 4 Ω and 6 Ω are connected in series. The equivalent resistance is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bzxqj8c",
      "content": "A) 2.4 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "f93g17m",
      "content": "B) 5 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "cqavxrj",
      "content": "C) 10 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "83kij13",
      "content": "D) 24 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5s88fjo",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (10 Ω)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2f9ecpp",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yucjoga",
      "content": "For series combination: R_total = R1 + R2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4t65vse",
      "content": "R_total = 4 + 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7h1amsl",
      "content": "R_total = 10 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8k7wyun",
      "content": "In series, resistance increases."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "MCQs",
      "id": "pgaien5"
    },
    {
      "id": "5o142ax",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xof5mkj",
      "content": "Two resistors of 6 Ω and 3 Ω are connected in parallel. The equivalent resistance is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7d28u7t",
      "content": "A) 1 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jp8ayy5",
      "content": "B) 2 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "te41r6t",
      "content": "C) 3 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pt32nja",
      "content": "D) 9 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gj02y2s",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B (2 Ω)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aon15a2",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zigq4by",
      "content": "For parallel combination:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "a1rxt0f",
      "content": "1/R = 1/R1 + 1/R2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n3c47o7",
      "content": "1/R = 1/6 + 1/3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "l9mv8pa",
      "content": "1/R = 1/6 + 2/6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xt5tb8l",
      "content": "1/R = 3/6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qt2k1ie",
      "content": "1/R = 1/2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "emttwsb",
      "content": "R = 2 Ω"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sum4e6g",
      "content": "In parallel, equivalent resistance is less than smallest resistor."
    },
    {
      "id": "ayujqr7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q4."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "skdwvpu",
      "content": "A device operates at 220 V and draws 2 A current. Its power is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ajaweaq",
      "content": "A) 110 W"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "vhjflmr",
      "content": "B) 220 W"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ns5hwqx",
      "content": "C) 440 W"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zrqgfbd",
      "content": "D) 880 W"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nz4pgkw",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (440 W)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lg0d88n",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "txpvig6",
      "content": "Formula: P = VI"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "uzxob2t",
      "content": "P = 220 × 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5ljamll",
      "content": "P = 440 W"
    },
    {
      "id": "iconmwx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q5."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "quo413b",
      "content": "A current of 5 A flows through a resistor of 4 Ω for 2 seconds. Heat produced is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Watch out for negative marking schemes typically associated with MCQ sections in competitive exams.",
        "Read question stems carefully for key qualifiers like 'NOT', 'INCORRECT', or 'ALWAYS'."
      ],
      "id": "2tsa01y"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g99fr8q",
      "content": "A) 100 J"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bt2qgwj",
      "content": "B) 150 J"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "f9b4ef5",
      "content": "C) 200 J"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "usjeynp",
      "content": "D) 250 J"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "z2otkjt",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (200 J)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9b3wwwu",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xqelli2",
      "content": "Using Joule’s Law: H = I²Rt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cam16a2",
      "content": "H = (5)² × 4 × 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m6vlrs1",
      "content": "H = 25 × 4 × 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zxl8x34",
      "content": "H = 200 Joule"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}